CM_ SG_ 2633880062 FmsStandardRequestsSupported "FMS-standard Requests Supported: Status signal which indicates if the FMS Vehicle Interface (FMS Gateway) will respond to requests from the FMS device for the PGs listed in the FMS Interface Specification.This mode is to support FMS  gateway devices ...";
CM_ SG_ 2633880062 FmsStandardSwVersionSupported "FMS-standard SW-version supported.: Information that identifies which issue level of the FMS-standard document the software included in the FMS gateway supports. Four bytes, representing xx.yy type revision level identification.Information to be ASCI...";
CM_ BO_ 2633883646 "Front Wheel Drive Status";
CM_ SG_ 2633883646 FrontWheelDriveActuatorStatus "Front Wheel Drive Actuator Status: Feedback on the front wheel drive actuator.00b = Front Wheel Drive Actuator not engaged01b = Front Wheel Drive Actuator engaged10b = Error11b = Not Available";
CM_ BO_ 2633911806 "Total Averaged Information";
CM_ SG_ 2633911806 EngineTotalAverageFuelEconomy "Engine Total Average Fuel Economy: Average fuel economy, equal to total vehicle distance divided by total fuel used, over the life of the engine";
CM_ SG_ 2633911806 EngineTotalAverageFuelRate "Engine Total Average Fuel Rate: Average fuel rate, equal to total fuel used divided by total engine hours, over the life of the engine";
CM_ BO_ 2633922558 "Auxiliary Pressures";
CM_ SG_ 2633922558 AuxiliaryGagePressureReading1 "Auxiliary Gage Pressure Reading 1: Identifies the current gage pressure (relative to atmosphere) that is configured uniquely per application.  Not to be used in place of defined parameters.";
CM_ SG_ 2633922558 AuxiliaryVacuumPressureReading "Auxiliary Vacuum Pressure Reading: Identifies the current vacuum pressure (relative to atmosphere) that is configured uniquely per application.  Not to be used in place of defined parameters.";
CM_ SG_ 2633922558 AxlrAsltPrssrRdng "Auxiliary Absolute Pressure Reading: Identifies the current absolute pressure (relative to 0 pressure) that is configured uniquely per application.  Not to be used in place of defined parameters.";
CM_ BO_ 2633922814 "Tire Pressure Control Unit Mode and Status";
CM_ SG_ 2633922814 DriveChannelMode "Drive Channel Mode: Indicates the functional mode of trailer/tag channel of the tire pressure control system.  0000b = Maintain0001b = Inflate0010b = Deflate0011b = Confirm0100b = Inflate Wait - System will inflate when conditions allow0101b = Deflat...";
CM_ SG_ 2633922814 PcuControlSolenoidStatus "PCU Control Solenoid Status: Current state of the control solenoid used to implement a tire pressure control system in its pneumatic control unit (PCU).00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633922814 PcuDeflateSolenoidStatus "PCU Deflate Solenoid Status: Current state of the deflate solenoid used to implement a tire pressure control system in its pneumatic control unit (PCU).00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633922814 PcuDriveSolenoidStatus "PCU Drive Solenoid Status: Current state of the drive solenoid used to implement a tire pressure control system in its pneumatic control unit (PCU).00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633922814 PcuSteerSolenoidStatus "PCU Steer Solenoid Status: Current state of the steer solenoid used to implement a tire pressure control system in its pneumatic control unit (PCU).00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633922814 PcuSupplySolenoidStatus "PCU Supply Solenoid Status: Current state of the supply solenoid used to implement a tire pressure control system in its pneumatic control unit (PCU).00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633922814 SteerChannelMode "Steer Channel Mode: Indicates the functional mode of steer channel of the tire pressure control system. 0000b = Maintain0001b = Inflate0010b = Deflate0011b = Confirm0100b = Inflate Wait - System will inflate when conditions allow0101b = Deflate Wait ...";
CM_ SG_ 2633922814 TirePressureCheckInterval "Tire Pressure Check Interval: The interval at which the system will check the tire pressures (e.g., 5, 10, 15 min.).NOTE - A value of 0 indicates continuous (real time) pressure readings.";
CM_ SG_ 2633922814 TirePressureSupplySwitchStatus "Tire Pressure Supply Switch Status: Current state of an open/closed type switch used to determine if adequate pressure exists for system implementation.00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633922814 TrailerTagChannelMode "Trailer/tag Channel Mode: Indicates the functional mode of trailer/tag channel of the tire pressure control system.0000b = Maintain0001b = Inflate0010b = Deflate0011b = Confirm0100b = Inflate Wait - System will inflate when conditions allow0101b = De...";
CM_ SG_ 2633922814 PTrlrTgOrPshSlndStts "PCU Trailer, Tag or Push Solenoid Status: Current state of the trailer, tag, or push solenoid used to implement a tire pressure control system in its pneumatic control unit (PCU).00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ BO_ 2633923070 "Tire Pressure Control Unit Target Pressures";
