CM_ SG_ 2633927934 AuxiliaryTemperature3 "Auxiliary Temperature 3: Temperature measured by auxiliary temperature sensor 3. Not to be used in place of existing SPs.";
CM_ BO_ 2633928446 "Service 2";
CM_ SG_ 2633928446 ServiceComponentIdentification "Service Component Identification: Identification of component needing service.  See Table SPN911_A.";
CM_ SG_ 2633928446 TimeSinceLastService "Time Since Last Service: The vehicle operation time since the last service was performed.  The type of service information is identified by the service component identification number.";
CM_ BO_ 2633929214 "Fuel Leakage";
CM_ SG_ 2633929214 EngineFluidBundLevel "Engine Fluid Bund Level: Ratio of the volume of engine fluid within the bund containment frame to the maximum capacity of the bund containment frame. The bund containment frame is used to contain engine fluid leaks including, but not limited to, engi...";
CM_ SG_ 2633929214 EngineFuelLeakage1 "Engine Fuel Leakage 1: Status signal which indicates fuel leakage in the fuel rail of the engine. Location can be either before or after the fuel pump.  00b = no leakage detected01b = leakage detected10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633929214 EngineFuelLeakage2 "Engine Fuel Leakage 2: Status signal which indicates fuel leakage in the fuel rail of the engine. Location can be either before or after the fuel pump.  00b = no leakage detected01b = leakage detected10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ BO_ 2633929470 "Engine Information 1";
CM_ SG_ 2633929470 EngineFuelRackPosition "Engine Fuel Rack Position: Measured position of the engine fuel rack.  A value of 0% rack represents no fueling and a value of 100% rack represents maximum fueling.";
CM_ SG_ 2633929470 EngineOilFilterIntakePressure "Engine Oil Filter Intake Pressure: Gage pressure of the engine oil before the oil reaches the oil filter.   See SPN 7470 for alternate resolution.";
CM_ SG_ 2633929470 EngnFlSstm1GsMssFlwRt "Engine Fuel System 1 Gas Mass Flow Rate: Gas mass flow rate delivered to an engine through its first fuel control system.  See SPN 3467 for the second fuel control system.";
CM_ SG_ 2633929470 InstntnsEstmtdBrkPwr "Instantaneous Estimated Brake Power: Estimate of the power developed by the engine.";
CM_ SG_ 2633929470 EngineExhaustBank1Pressure1 "Engine Exhaust Bank 1 Pressure 1: Gage pressure of the exhaust gases as measured at the turbine intake of the turbocharger. This SP to be used for inline engines or exhaust bank 1 of multiple bank engines.  See SPN 5749 for exhaust bank 2 and See SPN...";
CM_ BO_ 2633929726 "Engine Electrical System/Module Information";
CM_ SG_ 2633929726 ElectricalLoad "Electrical Load: Electrical power delivered by the engine to the electrical system connected to the generator.";
CM_ SG_ 2633929726 EngineTurningGearEngaged "Engine Turning Gear Engaged: Status signal which indicates that the turning gear is engaged.  The turning gear is used to turn the flywheel/crankshaft, for maintenance purposes, while the engine is not running.00b = Not engaged01b = Engaged10b = Erro...";
CM_ SG_ 2633929726 SafetyWireStatus "Safety Wire Status: Status signal which indicates that the safety wire has been activated.  When the safety wire is activated, the engine will not operate.  This is used for maintenance purposes.00b = Safety wire has not been activated01b = Safety wi...";
CM_ BO_ 2633930238 "Rebuild Information";
CM_ SG_ 2633930238 EngineOperationTimeSinceRebuild "Engine Operation Time Since Rebuild: The time in engine operation since the last engine rebuild.";
