CM_ BO_ 2633935102 "Articulation Control";
CM_ SG_ 2633935102 ArticulationAngle "Articulation Angle: Angle of deflection of an articulated transit vehicle (rotation angle about the vehicles z-axis). A right turn (clockwise) is indicated with a positive angle and a left turn is indicated with a negative angle.  This parameter is d...";
CM_ SG_ 2633935102 ArticulationAngularVelocity "Articulation Angular Velocity: Angular velocity of deflection of an articulated transit vehicle (rotation angle about the vehicle's z-axis).  An increasing clockwise angle is indicated with a positive angular velocity and an increasing counterclockwi...";
CM_ BO_ 2633935358 "Exhaust Oxygen 1";
CM_ SG_ 2633935358 EngineActualExhaust1Oxygen "Engine Actual Exhaust 1 Oxygen: The actual amount of oxygen in the exhaust represented as a percentage by volume with respect to the total volume of exhaust gases leaving the engine.Note:  A value of FB00h shall be provided when ambient or engine ope...";
CM_ SG_ 2633935358 EngineDesiredExhaustOxygen "Engine Desired Exhaust Oxygen: The desired amount of oxygen in the exhaust represented as a percentage by volume with respect to the total volume of exhaust gases leaving the engine.";
CM_ SG_ 2633935358 EngineDesiredRatedExhaustOxygen "Engine Desired Rated Exhaust Oxygen: The desired amount of oxygen in the exhaust at rated conditions represented as a percentage by volume with respect to the total volume of exhaust gases leaving the engine.";
CM_ SG_ 2633935358 EngnExhstO2SnsrClsdLpOprtn "Engine Exhaust O2 Sensor Closed Loop Operation: Indicates whether the engine is using the exhaust oxygen sensor to control the air/fuel ratio.00b = Engine not using the exhaust oxygen sensor (open loop)01b = Engine using the exhaust oxygen sensor for...";
CM_ SG_ 2633935358 EngnExhstO2SnsrFlngCrrtn "Engine Exhaust O2 Sensor Fueling Correction: The amount of fueling change required by the system based on the measured exhaust oxygen value compared to the maximum fueling change permitted by the system, expressed as percentages.";
CM_ BO_ 2633935614 "Alternate Fuel 2";
CM_ SG_ 2633935614 EFSstGsMssFwRtSsFCt "Engine Fuel System Gas Mass Flow Rate Sensor Fueling Correction: The amount of fuel the Gas Mass Flow Rate Sensor is sensing should be added or subtracted compared to the maximum amount of fuel the control system allows the sensor to add or subtract.";
CM_ SG_ 2633935614 EngnIntkMnfldDsrdAsltPrssr "Engine Intake Manifold Desired Absolute Pressure: The desired absolute intake manifold pressure (turbo boost limit) of the engine.";
CM_ SG_ 2633935614 EngnTrhrgrWstgtVlvPstn "Engine Turbocharger Wastegate Valve Position: The position of the turbocharger wastegate valve (not the electronic wastegate control valve).";
CM_ SG_ 2633935614 GaseousFuelCorrectionFactor "Gaseous Fuel Correction Factor: A correction to a predefined gaseous fuel energy (expressed in energy per unit volume) represented as a percentage.  The actual fuel energy used to control the engine is the product of the gaseous fuel correction facto...";
CM_ SG_ 2633935614 GssFlInjtnPlsCrrtnFtr "Gaseous Fuel Injection Pulse Correction Factor: A correction to the gaseous fuel injection pulse (expressed in msec) represented as a percentage.  100% means no correction, higher values indicate increased pulse time, lower values indicate decreased ...";
CM_ BO_ 2633935870 "Electronic Transmission Controller 6";
CM_ SG_ 2633935870 ClutchLifeRemaining "Clutch Life Remaining: Signal which indicates the actual clutch life remaining in percent. One hundred percent means the clutch is brand new and zero percent means the clutch is at the end of its life.";
CM_ SG_ 2633935870 HighestPossibleGear "Highest Possible Gear: The transmission calculates this gear continuously.  Together with the lowest possible gear (see  SPN 1114), it enables a management computer to know the exact range of available gears.Negative values are reverse gears, positiv...";
CM_ SG_ 2633935870 LowestPossibleGear "Lowest Possible Gear: The transmission calculates this gear continuously.  Together with the highest possible gear (see SPN 1115), it enables a management computer to know the exact range of available gears.Negative values are reverse gears, positive...";
CM_ SG_ 2633935870 RecommendedGear "Recommended Gear: The transmission calculates this gear continuously.  In dangerous situations this gear may be selected to gain back vehicle control.Negative values are reverse gears, positive values are forward gears, zero is neutral, 251 (FBh) is ...";
CM_ BO_ 2633936126 "Wheel Brake Lining Remaining Information 1";
CM_ SG_ 2633936126 BrkLnngRmnngFrntAxlLftWhl "Brake Lining Remaining, Front Axle, Left Wheel: The percentage of brake lining which can still be measured for the left wheel on the front axle.  100% represents new brake linings, 0% represents totally worn brake linings.";
CM_ SG_ 2633936126 BrkLnngRmnngFrntAxlRghtWhl "Brake Lining Remaining, Front Axle, Right Wheel: The percentage of brake lining which can still be measured for the right wheel on the front axle.  100% represents new brake linings, 0% represents totally worn brake linings.";
CM_ SG_ 2633936126 BrkLnngRmnngRrAxl1LftWhl "Brake Lining Remaining, Rear Axle #1, Left Wheel: The percentage of brake lining which can still be measured for the left wheel on the rear axle #1.  100% represents new brake linings, 0% represents totally worn brake linings.";
CM_ SG_ 2633936126 BrkLnngRmnngRrAxl1RghtWhl "Brake Lining Remaining, Rear Axle #1, Right Wheel: The percentage of brake lining which can still be measured for the right wheel on the rear axle #1.  100% represents new brake linings, 0% represents totally worn brake linings.";
CM_ SG_ 2633936126 BrkLnngRmnngRrAxl2LftWhl "Brake Lining Remaining, Rear Axle #2, Left Wheel: The percentage of brake lining which can still be measured for the left wheel on the rear axle #2.  100% represents new brake linings, 0% represents totally worn brake linings.";
CM_ SG_ 2633936126 BrkLnngRmnngRrAxl2RghtWhl "Brake Lining Remaining, Rear Axle #2, Right Wheel: The percentage of brake lining which can still be measured for the right wheel on the rear axle #2.  100% represents new brake linings, 0% represents totally worn brake linings.";
CM_ SG_ 2633936126 BrkLnngRmnngRrAxl3LftWhl "Brake Lining Remaining, Rear Axle #3, Left Wheel: The percentage of brake lining which can still be measured for the left wheel on the rear axle #3.  100% represents new brake linings, 0% represents totally worn brake linings.";
CM_ SG_ 2633936126 BrkLnngRmnngRrAxl3RghtWhl "Brake Lining Remaining, Rear Axle #3, Right Wheel: The percentage of brake lining which can still be measured for the right wheel on the rear axle #3.  100% represents new brake linings, 0% represents totally worn brake linings.";
CM_ BO_ 2633936894 "Fuel Consumption (Gaseous)";
CM_ SG_ 2633936894 TotalFuelUsedGaseous "Total Fuel Used (Gaseous): Total fuel consumed (trip drive fuel + trip PTO governor moving fuel + trip PTO governor non-moving fuel + trip idle fuel) over the life of the engine.";
CM_ SG_ 2633936894 TripFuelGaseous "Trip Fuel (Gaseous): Total fuel consumed (trip drive fuel + trip PTO governor moving fuel + trip PTO governor non-moving fuel + trip idle fuel) since the last trip reset.";
CM_ BO_ 2633937150 "Trip Time Information 2";
CM_ SG_ 2633937150 TripAirCompressorOnTime "Trip Air Compressor On Time: Total time that the air compressor is on and compressing air since the last trip reset.";
CM_ SG_ 2633937150 TripCruiseTime "Trip Cruise Time: Total time accumulated while the engine is in the cruise hold state, excluding time in accelerator override, since the last trip reset.";
CM_ SG_ 2633937150 TripEngineRunningTime "Trip Engine Running Time: Total time accumulated while the engine speed is greater than zero since the last trip reset.  Note that time with the ignition switch on but engine speed at zero is not included.";
CM_ SG_ 2633937150 TripIdleTime "Trip Idle Time: Total time accumulated while the engine speed is greater than zero, both the PTO and remote PTO governors are inactive, and the vehicle speed is less than 2 km/h, since the last trip reset.In marine applications, this parameter is def...";
CM_ SG_ 2633937150 TripPtoGovernorTime "Trip PTO Governor Time: Total time accumulated while the engine is in the PTO or remote PTO governor hold state since the last trip reset.";
CM_ BO_ 2633937406 "ECU History";
CM_ SG_ 2633937406 TotalEcuDistance "Total ECU Distance: Total distance accumulated over the life of the ECU.  When the ECU is replaced this value shall be reset.";
CM_ SG_ 2633937406 TotalEcuRunTime "Total ECU Run Time: Total time accumulated over the life of the ECU, from ignition switch ON to ignition switch OFF.  When the ECU is replaced this value shall be reset.";
CM_ BO_ 2633937662 "Fuel Information 1 (Gaseous)";
CM_ SG_ 2633937662 EngineFuelSpecificGravity "Engine Fuel Specific Gravity: This parameter conveys the specific gravity of the gaseous fuel being used by the engine.  The specific gravity of the fuel can then be used to compute the density of the fuel.";
CM_ SG_ 2633937662 TripAverageFuelRateGaseous "Trip Average Fuel Rate (Gaseous): Average fuel rate, equal to trip fuel divided by trip time while the engine speed is above zero, since the last trip reset.  This includes idle, engine PTO governor (both moving and non-moving) and drive operation bu...";
CM_ SG_ 2633937662 TtlEngnPtGvrnrFlUsdGss "Total Engine PTO Governor Fuel Used (Gaseous): Total fuel used while the PTO or remote PTO governors are in the hold state and engine speed is above zero, over the life of the engine.NOTE-This parameter is intended for gaseous fueled engines.  See SP...";
CM_ BO_ 2633937918 "Fuel Information 1 (Liquid)";
CM_ SG_ 2633937918 FlexibleFuelPercentage "Flexible Fuel Percentage: Measured signal that indicates the percentage of alcohol in the fuel currently being used.  0% means no alcohol in fuel, 100% means alcohol as fuel and nothing else.EXAMPLE: If a Bi-fuel vehicle has less than 10% ethanol in ...";
CM_ SG_ 2633937918 TotalEnginePtoGovernorFuelUsed "Total Engine PTO Governor Fuel Used: Total fuel used while the PTO or remote PTO governors are in the hold state and engine speed is above zero, over the life of the engine.NOTE-This parameter is intended for liquid fueled engines.  See SPN 1030 for ...";
CM_ SG_ 2633937918 TripAverageFuelRate "Trip Average Fuel Rate: Average fuel rate, equal to trip fuel divided by trip time while the engine speed is above zero, since the last trip reset.  This includes idle, engine PTO governor (both moving and non-moving) and drive operation but excludes...";
CM_ BO_ 2633938174 "Trip Time Information 1";
CM_ SG_ 2633938174 TripTimeInDerateByEngine "Trip Time in Derate by Engine: Total time accumulated when the engine final fueling has been derated due to an engine protection algorithm, since the last reset.";
CM_ SG_ 2633938174 TripTimeInGearDown "Trip Time in Gear Down: Total time accumulated when the vehicle has operated in one gear down from the top gear for a calibrated minimum time, since the last trip reset.";
CM_ SG_ 2633938174 TripTimeInTopGear "Trip Time in Top Gear: Total time accumulated when the vehicle has operated in top gear for a calibrated minimum time, since the last trip reset.";
CM_ SG_ 2633938174 TripTimeInVsl "Trip Time in VSL: Total time accumulated when the engine has operated on the vehicle speed limiter (VSL) while not in the cruise hold state, since the last trip reset.  The engine torque mode is equal to road speed governor during this operation.";
CM_ BO_ 2633938430 "Trip Shutdown Information";
CM_ SG_ 2633938430 TripNumberOfHotShutdowns "Trip Number of Hot Shutdowns: Total number of hot shutdowns since the last trip reset.  A hot shutdown is based on operation at high load or high engine speed or for long operating periods without allowing the engine to cool sufficiently.";
CM_ SG_ 2633938430 TripNumberOfIdleShutdowns "Trip Number of Idle Shutdowns: Total number of times the engine has been shutdown due to idling too long (at normal idle or fast idle) since the last trip reset.";
CM_ SG_ 2633938430 TripSuddenDecelerations "Trip Sudden Decelerations: Total number of decelerations whenever the vehicle deceleration is more than XYZ km/h/sec (where XYZ is a calibratible threshold), since the last trip reset.  A lengthy deceleration shall be counted as one sudden decelerati...";
CM_ SG_ 2633938430 TrpNmrOfIdlShtdwnOvrrds "Trip Number of Idle Shutdown Overrides: Total number of times an operator disables idle shutdown to prevent an engine shutdown, since the last trip reset.";
CM_ BO_ 2633938686 "Trip Vehicle Speed/Cruise Distance Information";
CM_ SG_ 2633938686 TripCruiseDistance "Trip Cruise Distance: Total distance that the engine has operated in the cruise hold state, excluding time in accelerator override, since the last trip reset.";
CM_ SG_ 2633938686 TripMaximumVehicleSpeed "Trip Maximum Vehicle Speed: Maximum vehicle speed achieved while the engine speed is greater than zero and the accelerator pedal position (APS) is at a value greater than 0%, since the last trip reset.";
CM_ BO_ 2633938942 "Engine Speed/Load Factor Information 1";
CM_ SG_ 2633938942 TotalEngineCruiseTime "Total Engine Cruise Time: Total time that the engine has operated in the cruise hold state, excluding time in accelerator override, over the life of the engine.";
CM_ SG_ 2633938942 TripAverageEngineSpeed "Trip Average Engine Speed: Average speed of the engine since the last trip reset.NOTE - Excludes ignition-on time without the engine speed above zero.  Includes idle, engine PTO governor (moving and non-moving), and drive operation.";
CM_ SG_ 2633938942 TripMaximumEngineSpeed "Trip Maximum Engine Speed: Maximum engine speed achieved since the last trip reset.";
CM_ SG_ 2633938942 TripDriveAverageLoadFactor "Trip Drive Average Load Factor: Average engine load factor while engine speed is greater than zero, vehicle speed is greater than or equal to 2 km/h, and both the PTO (moving/non-moving) and remote PTO governors are not in the hold state, since the l...";
CM_ SG_ 2633938942 TotalDriveAverageLoadFactor "Total Drive Average Load Factor: Average engine load factor while engine speed is greater than zero, vehicle speed is greater than or equal to 2 km/h, and both the PTO (moving/non-moving) and remote PTO governors are not in the hold state, over the l...";
CM_ BO_ 2633939198 "Trip Fuel Information (Gaseous)";
CM_ SG_ 2633939198 TripCruiseFuelUsedGaseous "Trip Cruise Fuel Used (Gaseous): Total fuel consumed while the engine is in the cruise hold state since the last trip reset.  If both cruise control and VSL (vehicle speed limiter) are commanding the same amount of fuel, the cruise control is deemed ...";
CM_ SG_ 2633939198 TripDriveFuelEconomyGaseous "Trip Drive Fuel Economy (Gaseous): Trip drive fuel economy is equal to the distance traveled by vehicle in the drive state (engine speed greater than zero, vehicle speed greater than or equal to 2 km/h, and neither the PTO or remote PTO governors are...";
CM_ SG_ 2633939198 TripDriveFuelUsedGaseous "Trip Drive Fuel Used (Gaseous): Total fuel consumed while the engine speed is greater than zero, vehicle speed is greater than or equal to 2 km/h, and neither the PTO or the remote PTO governors are controlling the engine power output, since the last...";
CM_ SG_ 2633939198 TripVehicleIdleFuelUsedGaseous "Trip Vehicle Idle Fuel Used (Gaseous): Total fuel consumed while neither the PTO or remote PTO governors are active, the engine speed is greater than zero, and vehicle speed is less than to 2 km/h, since the last trip reset.NOTE-This parameter is int...";
CM_ SG_ 2633939198 TrpPtGvrnrMvngFlUsdGss "Trip PTO Governor Moving Fuel Used (Gaseous): Total fuel consumed while the PTO or remote PTO governors are in the hold state, the engine speed is greater than zero, and vehicle speed is greater than or equal to 2 km/h, since the last trip reset.NOTE...";
CM_ SG_ 2633939198 TrpPtGvrnrNnMvngFlUsdGss "Trip PTO Governor Non-moving Fuel Used (Gaseous): Total fuel consumed while the PTO or remote PTO governors are in the hold state, the engine speed is greater than zero, and vehicle speed is less than to 2 km/h, since the last trip reset.NOTE-This pa...";
CM_ BO_ 2633939454 "Trip Fuel Information (Liquid)";
CM_ SG_ 2633939454 TripCruiseFuelUsed "Trip Cruise Fuel Used: Total fuel consumed while the engine is in the cruise hold state since the last trip reset.  If both cruise control and VSL (vehicle speed limiter) are commanding the same amount of fuel, the cruise control is deemed the active...";
CM_ SG_ 2633939454 TripDriveFuelEconomy "Trip Drive Fuel Economy: Trip drive fuel economy is equal to the distance traveled by vehicle in the drive state (engine speed greater than zero, vehicle speed greater than or equal to 2 km/h, and neither the PTO or remote PTO governors are controlli...";
CM_ SG_ 2633939454 TripDriveFuelUsed "Trip Drive Fuel Used: Total fuel consumed while the engine speed is greater than zero, vehicle speed is greater than or equal to 2 km/h, and neither the PTO or the remote PTO is controlling the engine power output, since the last trip reset.NOTE-This...";
CM_ SG_ 2633939454 TripPtoGovernorMovingFuelUsed "Trip PTO Governor Moving Fuel Used: Total fuel consumed while either the PTO or remote PTO governors are in the hold state, the engine speed is greater than zero, and vehicle speed is greater than or equal to 2 km/h, since the last trip reset.NOTE-Th...";
CM_ SG_ 2633939454 TripVehicleIdleFuelUsed "Trip Vehicle Idle Fuel Used: Total fuel consumed while neither the PTO or remote PTO governor is in the hold state, the engine speed is greater than zero, and vehicle speed is less than 2 km/h, since the last trip reset.In marine applications, this p...";
CM_ SG_ 2633939454 TrpPtGvrnrNnMvngFlUsd "Trip PTO Governor Non-moving Fuel Used: Total fuel consumed while either the PTO or remote PTO governors are in the hold state, the engine speed is greater than zero, and vehicle speed is less than 2 km/h, since the last trip reset.NOTE-This paramete...";
CM_ BO_ 2633939710 "Trip Distance Information";
CM_ SG_ 2633939710 TripDistanceInTopGear "Trip Distance in Top Gear: Total distance accumulated while the vehicle has operated in top gear for a calibrated minimum time since the last trip reset.";
CM_ SG_ 2633939710 TripDistanceOnVsl "Trip Distance on VSL: Total distance accumulated while the engine torque mode is road speed governing since the last trip reset.";
CM_ SG_ 2633939710 TripGearDownDistance "Trip Gear Down Distance: Total distance accumulated while the vehicle has operated in the gear which is one gear down from top gear and exceeds a calibrated minimum time (typically the time to shift the transmission) since the last trip reset.";
CM_ BO_ 2633939966 "Trip Fan Information";
CM_ SG_ 2633939966 TripFanOnTime "Trip Fan On Time: Total time the fan has been on (due to an automatic trigger or manual trigger) since the last trip reset.  The fan could be requested to be on by the engine system, a manual switch, and/or the A/C system.  Whichever system requests ...";
CM_ SG_ 2633939966 TripFanOnTimeDueToAManualSwitch "Trip Fan On Time Due to a Manual Switch: Total time the fan has been on due to manual activation by the operator (i.e., excluding time on due to automatic triggers) since the last trip reset.  For the time to be accumulated against the manual switch,...";
CM_ SG_ 2633939966 TripFanOnTimeDueToTheACSystem "Trip Fan On Time Due to the A/C System: Total time the fan has been on due to the A/C system since the last trip reset.  For the time to be accumulated against the A/C system, it is necessary that it be the first to request the fan activation or it b...";
CM_ SG_ 2633939966 TrpFnOnTmDTThEngnSstm "Trip Fan On Time Due to the Engine System: Total time the fan has been on due to engine triggers (i.e., excluding time on due to an operator manual switch or A/C system) since the last trip reset.  For the time to be accumulated against the engine sy...";
CM_ BO_ 2633940222 "Compression/Service Brake Information";
CM_ SG_ 2633940222 TotalCompressionBrakeDistance "Total Compression Brake Distance: Total distance over which the compression brakes have been active for the life of the engine.";
CM_ SG_ 2633940222 TripCompressionBrakeDistance "Trip Compression Brake Distance: Total distance over which the compression brakes have been active since the last trip reset.";
CM_ SG_ 2633940222 TripServiceBrakeApplications "Trip Service Brake Applications: Total number of times the service brakes have been activated since the last trip reset.  Brake applications of less than 0.5 s are not counted and lengthy brake applications (longer than 0.5 s) are counted as a single...";
CM_ SG_ 2633940222 TripServiceBrakeDistance "Trip Service Brake Distance: Total distance over which the service brakes have been active since the last trip reset.";
CM_ BO_ 2633940734 "Electronic Engine Controller 4";
CM_ SG_ 2633940734 EngineRatedPower "Engine Rated Power: Net brake power that the engine will deliver continuously, specified for a given application at a rated speed.";
CM_ SG_ 2633940734 EngineRatedSpeed "Engine Rated Speed: The maximum governed rotational velocity of the engine crankshaft under full load conditions.  Note that the engine speed at point 2 (SPN 528) is equal to rated engine speed only in the case when the engine has not been derated.  ...";
CM_ SG_ 2633940734 EngineRotationDirection "Engine Rotation Direction: Direction of engine rotation, as reported by the engine.  Direction convention as viewed by an observer standing at the rear of the engine, viewing the flywheel.00b = CounterClockWise (CCW)01b = ClockWise (CW)10b = Unknown ...";
CM_ SG_ 2633940734 EngnIntkMnfldPrssrCntrlMd "Engine Intake Manifold Pressure Control Mode: Indicates that the Boost Pressure Closed Loop Control status either open loop or closed loop.00b = Open loop 01b = Closed loop 10b = SAE reserved11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633940734 EngnPrlOlLwPrssrThrshld "Engine Prelube Oil Low Pressure Threshold: The minimum value that the engine oil pressure (SPN 100 and SPN 7468) must exceed in order to start the engine.This parameter is intended for applications that have an external means of lubricating the engin...";
CM_ SG_ 2633940734 CrnkAttmptCntOnPrsntStrtAttmpt "Crank Attempt Count on Present Start Attempt: Reports the number of cranking cycles undergone during the present start attempt.Note:  This is intended to be used in conjunction with Maximum Crank Attempts per Start Attempt, in order to give a FMI 0 d...";
CM_ BO_ 2633941758 "Electronic Retarder Controller 2";
CM_ SG_ 2633941758 CrsCntrlRtrdrAtvSpdOffst "Cruise Control Retarder Active Speed Offset: The additional speed (offset) above the operator selected cruise control set speed (SPN 6809 or SPN 86) at which the retarder will activate when cruise control is active. It is not an offset from SPN 7319 ...";
CM_ SG_ 2633941758 TransmissionOutputRetarder "Transmission Output Retarder: Identifies the status of the transmission output retarder.00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633941758 RetarderRoadSpeedLimitEnable "Retarder Road Speed Limit Enable: This indicates that the system is capable of activating the retarder to limit the downhill vehicle speed which is possible when SPN 4233 is ON and the operator has set a downhill vehicle speed.00b = Retarder Road Spe...";
CM_ SG_ 2633941758 RetarderRoadSpeedLimitActive "Retarder Road Speed Limit Active: This indicates the retarder road speed limit system is actively engaged and retarder is limiting the downhill vehicle speed. This parameter can also be used as feedback indication for conventional cruise control syst...";
CM_ SG_ 2633941758 TrnsmssnRtrdrEnlSwth "Transmission Retarder Enable Switch: The transmission retarder enable switch indicates whether the operator allows the transmission to engage its integral retarder when indicated by vehicle operating conditions.00b = Retarder Enable Switch Off01b = R...";
CM_ SG_ 2633941758 RetarderRoadSpeedLimitSetSpeed "Retarder Road Speed Limit Set Speed: Value of set (chosen) velocity of the retarder road speed limit system.";
CM_ SG_ 2633941758 RetarderRoadSpeedLimitReadiness "Retarder Road Speed Limit Readiness: This indicates that the system is capable of activating the retarder to limit the downhill vehicle speed. This parameter will be set to 01b when the system is capable of activating the retarder to limit the downhi...";
CM_ BO_ 2633942014 "Electronic Transmission Controller 5";
CM_ SG_ 2633942014 TransmissionLowRangeSenseSwitch "Transmission Low Range Sense Switch: Identifies the status of the switch that represents low range.00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633942014 TransmissionNeutralSwitch "Transmission Neutral Switch: Identifies the status of the switch that indicates neutral.00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633942014 TrnsmssnFrwrdDrtnSwth "Transmission Forward Direction Switch: Identifies the status of the switch that indicates forward direction.00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633942014 TrnsmssnHghRngSnsSwth "Transmission High Range Sense Switch: Identifies the status of the switch that represents high range.00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633942014 TrnsmssnRvrsDrtnSwth "Transmission Reverse Direction Switch: Identifies the status of the switch that indicates reverse direction.00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2633942014 TransmissionSplitterPosition "Transmission Splitter Position: The current position of the splitter cylinder.00b = Off/Low01b = On/High10b = Error11b = Not Available";
CM_ BO_ 2633942526 "Electronic Transmission Controller 4";
CM_ SG_ 2633942526 TrnsmssnSnhrnzrBrkVl "Transmission Synchronizer Brake Value: The current modulated value for the air supply to the synchronizer brake.";
CM_ SG_ 2633942526 TrnsmssnSnhrnzrClthVl "Transmission Synchronizer Clutch Value: The current modulated value for the air supply to the synchronizer clutch.";
