CM_ BO_ 2566520574 "APIs Supported";
CM_ SG_ 2566520574 EvApiId "EV API ID: ID value assigned to an API.If the SPN23215 (EV API Manufacturer ID) is zero, then this parameter will have one of the following values:0: Reserved for SAE J3271 CAN EVSE to EV API  1 - 250: Reserved for future useFor proprietary APIs, (i....";
CM_ SG_ 2566520574 EvApiManufacturerId "EV API Manufacturer ID: Manufacturer ID who maintains and publishes the API. A value of zero is reserved for standard interfaces whose API IDs, SPN 23214 (EV API ID), are managed by SAE.For proprietary API IDs, SPN 23214 (EV API ID), the Manufacturer...";
CM_ SG_ 2566520574 EvApiSupportedRoles "EV API Supported Roles: An API may have defined roles for the participants (e.g. Client-Server). This field indicates the roles supported by the CA. If an API has defined roles, then support for at least one of those roles must be indicated.0000b - T...";
CM_ SG_ 2566520574 EvApiMajorVersion "EV API Major Version: Major version for the API. APIs with differing major versions are not compatible.SP Position in PG  4, 12, .... 8n-4";
CM_ SG_ 2566520574 EvApiMinorVersion "EV API Minor Version: Minor version for the API.SP Position in PG  5, 13, .... 8n-3";
CM_ SG_ 2566520574 EvApiMinorVersionMinimum "EV API Minor Version Minimum: Minimum supported minor version of the this API that is compatible with the CA sending this PG.SP Position in PG  6, 14, .... 8n-2";
CM_ SG_ 2566520574 EvApiGrouping "EV API Grouping: Group number indicating sets of APIs that are mutually exclusive. Only one of the APIs from a set can be selected at a time.For example, an EVSE may support several different charging APIs, or charging API versions, but the EV can on...";
CM_ SG_ 2566520574 EvApiActiveByDefault "EV API Active By Default: If set, then this API will be active by default.Only one API in a API Grouping may have this bit set.SP Position in PG  7.5, 15.5, .... (8n-1).5";
